---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '20 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Tax for Taxi Drivers collects, uses and protects your personal data under UK GDPR."
>
  <section class="section privacy">
    <div class="wrap privacy-wrap">
      <div class="rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </div>

      <article class="rv prose">
        <p>
          Tax for Taxi Drivers (“we”, “us”, “our”) is based at Unit 4, North City Business Centre, 2 Duncairn Gardens,
          Belfast BT15 2GG. We provide accountancy and tax support services to self-employed clients, including taxi
          drivers, across Northern Ireland.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy explains how we handle personal data on this website, through our contact forms, and in our client
          portal, in line with UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.
        </p>

        <h2>What data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact enquiries</strong> — name, email, phone (optional), and your message when you use the
            contact form.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client portal</strong> — account details, tax submission information, and related documents you or
            our staff upload while using the portal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data</strong> — essential cookies and, if you opt in, optional analytics data about how
            the site is used.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why we use your data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to enquiries and provide our services (contract / legitimate interests).</li>
          <li>To operate the secure client portal and meet tax filing obligations (contract / legal obligation).</li>
          <li>To keep the website secure and improve it where you have consented to analytics (consent).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Lawful basis &amp; consent</h2>
        <p>
          Where we rely on consent (for example optional analytics cookies, or confirming you agree to this policy on
          the contact form), you can withdraw that consent at any time. Withdrawing consent does not affect the
          lawfulness of processing before withdrawal.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Essential cookies are required for security, forms, and the client portal. Optional analytics cookies are only
          set if you choose “Accept all” or enable Analytics in cookie preferences. You can change your choice at any
          time via “Cookie preferences” in the website footer.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
        <p>
          We use trusted processors to run this website and related services, including hosting, email delivery
          (Mailgun), and authentication / database hosting (Supabase) for the client portal. We do not sell your
          personal data. We may share information with HMRC or other authorities where required by law, or with our
          professional advisers under confidentiality.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
        <p>
          Contact enquiries are kept only as long as needed to respond and follow up. Client records are retained for
          the periods required for tax and accounting purposes, then securely deleted or anonymised.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access your personal data</li>
          <li>Correct inaccurate data</li>
          <li>Request erasure or restriction in certain cases</li>
          <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
          <li>Data portability where processing is automated and consent/contract based</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent where we rely on it</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below. You can also complain to the Information
          Commissioner’s Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:info@taxfortaxidrivers.co.uk">info@taxfortaxidrivers.co.uk</a> or call the office on{' '}
          <a href="tel:02890132083">02890 132083</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Postal address: Unit 4, North City Business Centre, 2 Duncairn Gardens, Belfast BT15 2GG.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 52px);
    margin: 14px 0 10px;
  }

  .meta {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 16.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--yellow-deep);
  }
</style>
